        "comment": "Static unpacking and C2 recovery, 2026-10-25 UTC. SHA-256 verified; 449,090-byte community ELF first_seen 2026-10-25 07:15:36 UTC. A JSON trailer starts at file offset 448,752; its 337-character JSON object occupies a 338-byte tail including the final newline. Fields are config/id/enckey/ParentId/ip/ParentIp/ParentHostname. Identifier, encryption and host-metadata values are omitted, and ip/ParentIp are not automatically classified as C2. Removing this trailer inside an isolated inspection sandbox allows trusted UPX decompression: unpacked core SHA-256 7d544e1c6d2e27906d3164c506d6778f901ea959d4d8b7e8a0f6b3cf6cef7c7a, 1,288,624 bytes. It contains primary HTTP C2 http://103.176.111.176/cgi-bin/p.cgi at file offset 0x136140 (VA 0x537140). Default-selection code references/copies that field at 0x41a0b2-0x41a0cf. Check-in formatting at 0x41ab10-0x41ab1f reaches the HTTP routine at 0x41ab3d. This differs from earlier a016f637.../90950ae9... records that used 177.221.180.26. Broader executable/read-only section hashes also differ; do not claim these builds differ only in the primary-IP field. The JSON schema and p.cgi protocol support Prometei lineage. Dummy.zero, a legacy 16-character onion name and an I2P literal are preserved as contextual strings, not claims of usable/current infrastructure. This is a recent compiled configuration observation, not a live bot session or verified endpoint availability. No malware/packer-stub execution, C2 connection or delivery-server retrieval; temporary decompressed files remained non-executable. No raw trailer values are included."
